  "title": "AMRI 16-N-0031 sleep1",
  "description": "Overnight simultaneous EEG-fMRI recordings from a pilot sleep study (sleep1) conducted at the Advanced MRI section of NINDS, NIH, around 2016-2017. Subjects were scanned for approximately 8 hours across two consecutive nights and were aroused at random intervals eight times per night. The dataset is the pilot for the later sleep2 study.",
  "methods_description": "Participants underwent simultaneous EEG and fMRI for about 8 hours on each of two consecutive nights, with 8 randomly timed arousals during the night.",
